> What is guaranteed, and the zero/255 exception

For one altered input bit, the integer byte change is δ=±2^b for 0≤b≤7. None of these
values is zero modulo 255, so A changes and the raw tag must change, independently
of the position or the message length. This assumes the original tag is held fixed.
A simultaneous change to data and the transmitted tag is a different error model.

A general single-byte replacement instead has δ between −255 and 255. Apart from
an unchanged byte, its only nonzero multiple of 255 is the change between zero and 255.
Thus the original blanket claim about all single-byte errors was false. The following
complete census includes every possible replacement at one zero byte: 255 changed
candidates, of which 254 change the tag and the replacement 255 is missed. Candidate
zero is an unchanged control and is not counted as an undetected error.

The raw container has sixteen bits, but only 255²=65,025 canonical residue pairs.
This count alone does not establish a collision probability for arbitrary inputs.
Both empty input and every all-zero/all-255 sequence have raw tag zero. Leading a
message with zero or 255 also leaves this zero-initialised raw checksum unchanged;
the tag therefore does not independently bind a message length.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fletcher_alias.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
const std::string zero(1,'\0'),ff(1,static_cast<char>(255));const auto c=dm::algorithms::fletcher16_replacement_scan(zero,0);
  std::print("Zero / 255 raw Fletcher tags: {} / {}; plain byte sums {} / {}.\n",dm::algorithms::fletcher16(zero),dm::algorithms::fletcher16(ff),dm::algorithms::byte_sum32(zero),dm::algorithms::byte_sum32(ff));
  std::print("Complete one-position replacement census: candidates {}; changed {}; detected {}; changed but missed {}; byte folds {}.\n\n",c.replacements.size(),c.changed,c.detected,c.missed,c.bytes_processed);
  std::print("| replacement octet | changed byte | changed raw tag | raw tag |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");for(unsigned value:{0,1,254,255}){const auto&r=c.replacements[value];std::print("| {} | {} | {} | 0x{:04X} |\n",value,r.changed,r.detected,r.checksum);}
  const auto prefixed=dm::algorithms::fletcher16(std::string("\0abcde",6));std::print("\nLeading-zero control: abcde 0x{:04X}; zero+abcde 0x{:04X}; equal {}.\n",dm::algorithms::fletcher16("abcde"),prefixed,prefixed==dm::algorithms::fletcher16("abcde"));
  std::vector<double>x,y;for(const auto&r:c.replacements){x.push_back(r.replacement);y.push_back(r.detected?1:0);}
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(x,y,"All candidates",{37,99,235},2.5).points({0,255},{0,0},"Unchanged tag",{220,38,38},5).text(42,.18,"0: unchanged control",{100,116,139},17).text(205,.18,"255: changed, missed",{220,38,38},17).title("A complete zero-byte replacement census").x_label("Replacement octet value").y_label("Raw tag changes (1=yes)").x_limits(-5,260).y_limits(-.2,1.5).legend({"Tag changed","No tag change: 0 or 255"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).size(900,500).save_svg("build/fletcher_alias.svg");
  if(c.changed!=255||c.detected!=254||c.missed!=1||prefixed!=0xC8F0)throw std::runtime_error("modulo255 alias");
}
