> Position sensitivity has exact transposition aliases

Suppose i<j initially contain bytes a,b. Exchanging them leaves A unchanged, while

$$
\Delta B=(j-i)(b-a)\pmod{255}.
$$
\alttext(The modular change in B for a transposition is the position separation times the difference of the two byte values, modulo two hundred and fifty-five.)

An adjacent exchange of distinct octets is detected except for the zero/255 pair.
At greater distances, 255=3×5×17 has zero divisors. A distance of three and a byte
difference of 85 give a product of 255 and an unchanged raw tag, even when neither
byte is zero or 255. For example, [1,0,0,86] and [86,0,0,1] both produce 0x5A57.
Other examples are distance five with difference 51, distance seventeen with difference
15, and distance 255 with difference one. Position-sensitive does not mean every
reordering is detected.

The scalar delta API evaluates that exact modular formula. The table independently
recomputes both complete messages through the native checksum. The figure queries
the formula over distances 1 through 255 and marks its zeros, identifying the gaps
at which those specified exchanges are missed. These are exact conditions, not sampled
error probabilities.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fletcher_transpositions.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
std::print("| distance | octet difference | original raw tag | swapped raw tag | predicted delta B | detected |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
  for(auto [distance,gap]:std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,unsigned>>{{1,1},{3,85},{5,51},{17,15},{255,1}}){std::string data(distance+1,'\0');data[0]=1;data[distance]=static_cast<char>(1+gap);const auto swapped=dm::algorithms::checksum_swap_bytes(data,0,distance);const auto a=dm::algorithms::fletcher16(data),b=dm::algorithms::fletcher16(swapped),delta=dm::algorithms::fletcher16_transposition_delta(distance,1,static_cast<std::uint8_t>(1+gap));std::print("| {} | {} | 0x{:04X} | 0x{:04X} | {} | {} |\n",distance,gap,a,b,delta,a!=b);if((a!=b)!=(delta!=0))throw std::runtime_error("transposition delta identity");}
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<unsigned>gaps{1,15,51,85};const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB>colors{{37,99,235},{22,163,74},{234,88,12},{124,58,237}};
  std::print("\n| octet difference | undetected distances in 1..255 |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t row=0;row<gaps.size();++row){std::vector<double>x,y;for(std::uint64_t d=1;d<=255;++d)if(dm::algorithms::fletcher16_transposition_delta(d,1,static_cast<std::uint8_t>(1+gaps[row]))==0){x.push_back(d);y.push_back(row);}std::print("| {} | {} |\n",gaps[row],x.size());p.points(x,y,"",colors[row],4);}
  p.title("Exact distances where the transposition leaves the tag unchanged").x_label("Position separation, in bytes").y_label("Octet difference").y_tick_labels({"1","15","51","85"}).x_limits(-3,263).y_limits(-.5,3.5).size(950,480).save_svg("build/fletcher_transpositions.svg");
}
